00:00:39.989 --> 00:00:44.010
to impress a lender or avoid taxation.

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:49.780
Specifically, ProPublica has documents that
relate to a, they relate to, I believe it's

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:53.489
for Manhattan buildings that Donald Trump
owns.

00:00:53.489 --> 00:00:57.719
And they obtained these documents through
freedom of information act requests.

00:00:57.719 --> 00:01:04.179
And the documents were provided because, uh,
these documents were made public because Trump

00:01:04.179 --> 00:01:09.649
appealed his property tax for the buildings
in question every year for, in some cases,

00:01:09.649 --> 00:01:11.560
nine years in a row.

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:17.639
And so what ProPublica was able to do, very
solid investigation was take the tax records

00:01:17.639 --> 00:01:22.810
and compare them with loan records, uh, that
Donald Trump's lender, ladder Capitol made

00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:25.810
public when they sold the, the debt.

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:32.040
But this isn't just generally saying to a
lender, Oh, my building's worth 50 million.

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:35.849
And then saying to the IRS, the building's
